WEBVTT

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.050
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:06.930
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.470
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.830
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.900
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:38.100
dokoka tooku de mimi wo sumashiteru hito ga iru
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:46.070
arayuru basho de sora wo miageteru hito ga iru
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:53.900
yozora no shita de kuchibue fuiteru bokutachi wa
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:00:54.990 --> 00:01:01.660
kotoba mo nai mama yubi de tada seiza wo nazotteru
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:09.130
samugariya no yume tsumetai kimi no te
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:18.510
atatameru mahou wa hitotsu no michi wo shinjiru koto
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:27.270
houkigumo no mukou ni mitsuketa hitotsubu no hoshi wa
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.530
kagayaku hoshi demo kasukana hoshi demo
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.490
kimi dake no hikari
is the light of only you.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.270
mune no kumo no mukou ni mienai mama no michishirube
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:43.080
is a sign post that remains unseen.
mune no kumo no mukou ni mienai mama no michishirube

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:50.800
saa kono te wo hiraite ima nani wo shinjimasuka?
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.470
Kazuma and Kawachi, who made it to their first
day of work at Pantasia’s southern Tokyo store,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.510
met Matsushiro Ken, the manager.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.440
Delicious!

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.190
The horse ate the bread!

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:19.360
Matsushiro told the two to make a delicious
French bread that even a horse would eat.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:19.830
Delicious bread
Matsushiro told the two to make a delicious
French bread that even a horse would eat.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:20.410
Delicious bread

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.170
At the same time, he declared that he would cancel their employment

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:25.630
if they could not do it
by the following day.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.170
Kawachi had difficulty accepting this,

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.500
but there was a profound reason behind
the condition that Matsushiro set out.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.760
I believe the manager is concerned about allergies.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:41.260
In other words, the “delicious bread”
that the manager speaks of...

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.720
is made without milk or butter,
all without sacrificing flavor,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.390
while bringing good health and good taste together...

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.480
The ultimate bread, right?

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.230
De-licious!!

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.280
A Decisively Ultimate Butter!

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.000
Right!

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.410
S-She died...

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.430
This guy’s really sentimental...

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.510
I mean, I told you she’s not dead.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:15.590
O-Onee-chan!

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.960
I’m telling you, she’s not dead!
O-Onee-chan!

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.470
Geez...

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.810
It seems you enjoy gossiping, as usual...

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.140
young lady.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.230
Manager!

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.450
Can’t you be a bit more stylish?

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.080
But still, Manager,
I don’t dislike your spirit.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.330
I’ll make it...

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:47.200
French bread that’s tasty, good for the
body, and that even a horse would eat.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:50.960
Huh?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.800
It’s Arabian oil shock.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.330
You must be careful of Arabian oil shock.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:55.840
Note: “Anafirakishii shokku” (anaphylactic shock) sounded to Kazuma like “Arabia sekiyu shokku.” (Arabian oil shock)

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.680
Arabian oil shock?

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.840
You out of toilet paper or something?

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.020
Eh?

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.840
Huh? Little sister?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.520
That’s why you’ve also got to
be wary of milk, Nee-chan.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:07.730
Milk?

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.140
Kazuma, surely...

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.900
you’re not talking about anaphylactic shock, are you?

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:12.860
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.230
In that case, you don’t have to worry about it.
I don’t think that’s a problem for us.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.820
Why?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.660
Usually, in our case, we tend to
drink Hanako’s milk, don’t we?

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.830
That girl has big breasts, so she produces
a lot of milk every day...

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.200
Hanako’s big breasts...

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.290
Hanako’s milk.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.540
Hello?

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.750
Hey!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.880
That’s it!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:33.170
Hanako’s milk!

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.620
Uh, what?

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.340
Public Telephone
Hanako’s milk!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:37.630
It’s decided!
Public Telephone

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.340
Hanako’s milk.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.720
Nee-chan, send some of Hanako’s milk over.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:42.630
Fresh stuff.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.510
Huh?

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.180
I need it right away.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.270
Please, send it through a home-delivery service.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.270
Well, I don’t mind that, but...

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.640
I need it by tomorrow.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.480
That’s impossible! Geez...

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.980
There’s no way they’d deliver it within a day.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.740
Oh, really? I thought that it
would arrive within 5 hours.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.360
Of course that’s impossible!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.070
We’re way out in the country, you know.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.700
No way...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.860
Oh well.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.540
In that case, leave it to me.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.790
Leave what?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:11.960
Have you forgotten...

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.120
about my cute Tetsuko #3?

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.580
Ah, that!

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.510
But then you’d be...

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.340
Idiot.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.300
You don’t have to worry about it.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.590
Don’t think about inconveniences to your family.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.340
Just do what you can right now.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:28.840
Okay!

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.430
Things I can do right now...

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.320
Things I can do right now...

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:43.780
Things I can do right now...

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.900
Things I can do right now...

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.080
This is it.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.830
I’ve got to use this.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:58.010
Just watch, I’ll make delicious Kawachi-style
bread and astound him!

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.050
Things I can do right now...

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:05.920
Oh, Azuma.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.920
It seems that you’ve also thought of something.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.970
I’d like to commend you, but...

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.060
Things I can...

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.560
do right now!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.560
T-That’s...!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.110
Um, what?

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.960
What’s with that?

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.190
What’s with what?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.820
I thought you came up with a secret
plan for making delicious bread,

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:32.410
but you ran out of time, so you gave up, and
instead of “yake-zake,” it’s “yake-juice?!”

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.290
At this rate, you’ll be fired by that ossan.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.700
What are you saying?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.250
I’m just doing what I can do right now.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:40.790
Eh?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:41.380
See ya!

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:42.710
Hey!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.090
What about making delicious bread?

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.260
I was wrong about you, Azuma...

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:51.430
I never would have thought that you’d be that gutless.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.680
Oh well, never mind.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.390
In that case, I’ll be the only one making delicious bread,

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.810
and become recognized by the manager.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.190
Just wait, Pantasia main store.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.480
I’ll be big!

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.660
It’s just as I thought.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.130
The manager made delicious bread using this, too.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.250
Moreover, with these ingredients...

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.630
even a horse would eat it.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.640
Azuma-san isn’t here.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.310
Is Azuma-san not going to make any delicious bread?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.530
Um...

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.110
Azuma-san, what are you doing in front of the store?

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.110
I’m doing what I can do right now.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:54.620
Huh?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.880
Because this is all I can do right now.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.840
I wonder what happened...?

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.550
Time’s running out, too...

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.250
It’s here!

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:11.090
There’s no mistaking it, it’s Tetsuko #3!

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:11.850
What?

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.100
Yo. Thanks for waiting.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.650
Nee-chan.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:27.820
Onee-san?

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.730
Hmmm?

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:34.740
Pantasia’s famous and all, but even
the main store is this small?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:35.740
Um...

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.450
This isn’t the main store...

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.660
Never mind that, Nee-chan.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:40.960
I know, I know.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.750
Here. Hanako’s milk.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.710
I raced over here, so it’s totally fresh.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.580
Thank you!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.210
Hanako’s... milk?

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:08.980
Horse Race

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.200
What is it?

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.500
What kind of question is that?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.910
I made it... A delicious bread.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:27.580
Just in time, huh?

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.460
Where’s the little kid?

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.130
Who knows.
I’m not exactly his guardian.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.170
I see.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.140
That aside, Manager, will you have a look at my bread?

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:42.010
Like yours, it’s a delicious bread made while
taking allergies into consideration,

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:46.060
without the use of any dairy products
such as milk or butter.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.650
This is delicious bread... made Kawachi-style!

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.360
With this French bread...
I’ll be raised in public esteem,

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.450
which means proper employment,

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.740
which also means Manager’s favor,

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.700
which means going to the main store.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:05.040
My aspirations are within reach.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.920
That moron’s late again?

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.420
He’s really got some nerve.

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:17.890
Nee-chan, thank you.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:18.450
Sure.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:21.760
Wow, it took longer than I expected.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.730
I was making butter.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.390
Butter?!

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.700
Whew, if was hard labor.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.660
Making butter is
quite troublesome, isn’t it?

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:33.730
I had to shake it in a PET bottle with all I had.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.580
PET bottle?!

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.500
So that’s why he drank the juice in one go that time...

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.700
And the unnecessary carbon dioxide...

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.710
Yeah! Thanks to that,
my stomach is still bloated.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:46.300
I understand what you used the PET bottle for.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.920
But what’s the meaning of this?

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.180
What were you thinking when you made butter?

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:53.290
As I said, I was making butter to put in this bread.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:55.560
You want to get your ass kicked?!

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.810
W-What are you saying?

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:59.590
You were listening to the story about
the manager’s sister, weren’t you?

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:02.430
I did some research.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:05.480
Alpha-S1 casein,
which is contained in milk,

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.070
is the main cause of allergic reactions.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:10.740
Since butter is made from milk, it’d be the same.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.440
You were aware of this,
yet you’re still using if?

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:16.080
Though you’re a moron, I still thought
you had some consideration.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.570
I misjudged you, Azuma.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.330
Don’t get the wrong idea!

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.780
What I used may have been butter, but...

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:28.880
It’s butter made from Hanako,
a goat’s milk...

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:29.790
Goat butter!

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.040
Goat?

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:38.000
And this bread which contains that butter is...

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:43.090
<i>Japan</i> #24’s variant...

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:45.400
France-<i>Japan</i>!

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:57.500
<i>Japan</i> #24’s variant...

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.610
France-<i>Japan</i>!

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:01.320
Goat?

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.280
France-<i>Japan</i>...
An enhanced <i>Japan</i>.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:07.080
But, goat or otherwise,
milk is still milk.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.290
What... I’m... saying... is...

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.540
you’re still using milk!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.040
Take this!

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:18.510
Full marks!

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:19.890
Leave this moron alone,

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:21.600
and take a look at my bread.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.800
Have a taste of delicious bread made Kawachi-style.

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:29.970
Oats, huh?

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:34.190
That’s right, your delicious bread
also has oats in it, right?

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.070
The reason the crust is so fragrant

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:38.660
is because the bread dough was sprinkled with oats.

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:40.950
These oats are a nutritious food source,

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:44.200
containing an abundance of vitamin C,
beta-carotene, and calcium,

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.700
which are needed by our bodies.

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.460
Moreover, horses love it.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:49.630
In other words...

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.170
Delicious!

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:00.480
That means he’ll eat it.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.920
What do you think, Manager?

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:05.650
Azuma!

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:07.180
What is it, Kawachi?

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.290
Give me that.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:13.600
Here!

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.800
Goat’s milk or whatever, the horse
won’t eat Azuma’s bread.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.750
It got stomped on, it’s the worst!

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:43.300
What on earth...
have you guys been doing?

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:47.320
Did you come to Tokyo
to make horse feed?

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.700
I forgot...

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:49.300
Huh?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.510
I completely forgot about the horse.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.010
So, it seems that

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:57.370
even the horse could tell the quality difference
between Azuma’s bread and mine...

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:00.650
But unfortunately,
my bread is incomplete.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:05.130
Without adding milk or butter,
it’ll always be a level below your bread.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:06.590
Even if I get the fragrance of the crust,

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:09.660
I can’t create the dough loved by Japanese:
dough that is soft inside.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.600
I shall teach you.

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.140
It’s natural yeast.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:14.600
Natural yeast, you say?!

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:18.080
However, it’s not your average
natural yeast!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:22.250
The natural yeast I use to make my bread rise, is...

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.260
hatsuga... genmai... koubo!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.320
And, the final creation is...

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:36.590
Oat hatsuga genmai koubo French bread!

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:41.670
O-Oat hatsuga genmai koubo French bread, he says?!

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:43.280
A-And naked, too?

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:44.790
Who is?

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:45.780
H-Huh?

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:49.510
Such power, it seems that he made me hallucinate.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:52.280
The aura about this guy isn’t normal.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:54.350
N-Never mind.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:56.830
I’ll tell you this, since you raised
the topic of natural yeast...

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:01.390
I have tried using natural yeast made from raisins and other various sources in the past.

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:02.400
I don’t quite understand,

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.670
but I didn’t think it’d be so different
using hatsuga genmai yeast.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.300
You fool!

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.950
Hatsuga genmai is the source of life.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:20.200
That energy

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:24.300
gives birth to the best dough, dough
that always remains soft!

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.500
W-What’s this?!

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.930
I shall explain.
Hatsuga genmai is

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:44.190
brown rice that’s in the state of germination
between 0.5 and 1mm.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:47.440
Compared with normal brown rice, it’s soft and sweet, and makes a high-quality yeast.

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:51.220
The nutritional value is extremely high, and
it could even be called the source of life.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:53.390
The effect of that is as follows...

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:57.080
Number one!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.900
Thanks to the gamma-aminobutyric acid,
high blood pressure is lowered.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.230
B-Blood pressure...

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:06.580
Number two!

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:10.490
The abundant dietary fiber helps prevent
constipation and colon cancer.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:15.320
I suddenly need to go to the toilet...

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.680
Number three!

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:21.330
A powerful, abundant antioxidant prevents
the buildup of excess oxygen.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:26.300
I-I’m suffocating...

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.040
The finishing blow!

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:33.860
Number four!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:39.120
It contains minerals that are absorbed well,
such as potassium, zinc and calcium.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:56.960
You will now...

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:58.000
germinate.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:04.520
H-Hatsuga genmai, banzai...

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:24.350
Hey, Kansai-ben.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:26.210
Is something wrong?

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.360
No, not really.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:31.250
He made me hallucinate again...

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.930
However, to think that such an
incredible yeast existed...

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:39.050
It’s hard to admit, but even I couldn’t reach that level.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:42.720
Still, the manager’s impression of me couldn’t be bad.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:43.640
At the very least,

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:46.620
my bread was better than Azuma’s,
which the horse wouldn’t eat.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:49.100
I guess I won.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:53.570
With this, I’m not just from a branch store,
I’m a proper artisan of Pantasia.

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:56.220
By the way...

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.480
Why did you use butter?

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.700
Jii-chan was telling me...

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:07.210
After the war, there wasn’t much
cow’s milk around Japan,

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.310
so goat’s milk was more commonly used.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:14.030
Because of that, Jii-chan and the others
didn’t have allergic reactions to milk.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:15.590
I see.

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:18.840
Certainly, goat’s milk does not contain alpha-S1 casein,

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.510
which is the main cause of allergies in cow’s milk.

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:24.970
It’s supposedly quite close in composition
to human breast milk.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.020
S-So that’s why Azuma used goat’s milk?

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:28.920
Kansai-ben.

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:30.820
Give me his bread.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.330
Umm... How is it?

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:46.040
Hmm... Goat, eh?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.010
No, no no!

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:02.120
These aren’t the constellations I’m after.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.610
T-This is it!

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:14.130
Capricorn!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.270
De-licious!

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.490
This is...

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:25.370
de-licious!

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.330
If the manager’s bread is delicious bread,

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.440
then Azuma’s France-<i>Japan</i> is surely the same.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:33.830
The slight acidity and mellow scent
that cow’s milk doesn’t have!

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:36.530
I didn’t know that goat’s milk
was this great!

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:39.590
There is another fine point in goat’s milk.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:42.430
And that is... the size of the fat particles.

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:44.140
Fat particles?

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:46.930
The fat particles in goat’s milk are
smaller than those in cow’s milk.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.930
Due to that, more of the particles
are able to penetrate the dough,

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:53.580
and a bread with a fuller, richer taste is produced.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:57.900
Also, goat’s milk contains about 20 times
more taurine than cow’s milk,

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.590
and even has great nutritional value.

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:02.860
O-Oh, really...

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:04.350
Fearsome goat’s milk.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:05.810
However, it’s no good.

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:09.120
The horse wouldn’t eat it. That’s why it’s no good.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:12.250
I was so concerned with the taste and allergies...

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:13.810
that I forgot about the horse.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.710
T-That’s right. It’s no good, that’s what I think.

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.000
That is...

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.200
not true at all!

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:22.920
I was particular about the
“delicious bread,”

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:26.220
but you made a bread that exceeded my expectations.

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:28.700
Note: Similar to the horse joke, this time
it’s a goat sound effect joke.
That is... de-licious bread!

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:33.940
If your wish is for as many people as possible
to be able to enjoy your delicious bread...

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.210
whether or not a horse would eat it is irrelevant.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:41.970
You have opened a new path by
different means than I had...

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:44.400
You’re on the frontier, so to speak.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.970
Frontier?

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:49.200
T-That’s right, Azuma did well, too.

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:50.700
Not as well as me, though...

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.450
Even a monkey can be a mimic!

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:52.980
Whoa!

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.040
But we bread artisans cannot be that way.

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:58.420
You must never forget that frontier spirit,

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:00.590
and break into a new world.

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:03.950
Show more confidence!
And then, push forward!

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.760
If you believe in yourself and
push onwards, then surely...

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:11.200
surely a day will come when you find your ideal bread!

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.110
My ideal bread...

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:29.350
I... will work hard, Manager!

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.750
Uhh... When he mentioned the mimic,
was he referring to me?

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:39.420
Azuma’s receiving some serious praise.

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:42.920
What... What’ll happen to me, Manager?

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:43.960
Hey, you...

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.840
My brother’s senpai from the bread shop.

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:49.140
Well, I’ll be counting on you to look after my brother.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:51.620
No way...

00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:57.000
Hey, you guys.

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:01.960
Welcome to Pantasia’s
southern Tokyo store.

00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:04.010
Does that mean...?

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:06.260
Yes. You’re both recruited.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:07.970
Yes!

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:11.820
An interesting pair has arrived this year...

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:12.990
And...

00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:15.560
to think that one possesses Solar Hands...

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:20.420
My store will be interesting from now on.

00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:25.320
Umm... Tsukino-san.

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:29.030
When will those two actually do some work for us?

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:32.560
Who knows?

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:46.640
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:55.650
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:06.660
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:11.830
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:17.970
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.540
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:24.680
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:29.450
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:33.290
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:37.990
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:43.160
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:43.430 --> 00:23:51.970
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:52.370 --> 00:24:01.330
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:07.720
Whoa, who’s this ossan?

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:08.300
He is...

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:11.550
St. Pierre’s Mokoyama Tsuyoshi!

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:12.740
Gah, yet another?!

00:24:12.740 --> 00:24:14.450
T-That guy is...?!

00:24:14.450 --> 00:24:16.390
Next episode, Yakitate!! Japan.

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:18.580
It’s the Main Store!!
Dancing Meister!

00:24:18.580 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to see it!

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.160 --> 00:24:25.040
The reason bread expands so much

00:24:25.040 --> 00:24:27.420
is because the yeast in the dough breathes,

00:24:27.420 --> 00:24:29.880
and puffs out carbon dioxide!

00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:31.740
Hi, hi, fuu...

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:33.010
I see!
